;; The RESUMABLE validator session (P6.2; owner direction D027, architecture
;; §17 rev 3; D029/D030; design D090-D095): one message of a DECLARED length
;; validated against one rule of a verified Program over WINDOWS of it. Each
;; vms-step call is given a window [base, base + len) and runs until the
;; verdict (the code, out filled as vm-validate fills it), until it needs bytes
;; the window does not hold (VMS_NEED: vms-need-offset / vms-need-length), or
;; until it has done its work quantum (VMS_YIELD: give a window holding
;; vms-position). It never calls the host. Verdict, reason, subcode, offset,
;; budget used, items and path are vm-validate's whatever the windows and the
;; quantum (bb vmsession-test).
;;
;; The walk is the buffer walk's, item by item (D091): an item the window holds
;; whole (by a structural prescan, bounded by the window and the quantum) is
;; evaluated by snug.vm.eval / snug.vm.dead THEMSELVES; an item that crosses gets
;; a frame (snug.vm.scont, snug.vm.sstr) that runs the generic path phase by
;; phase with the same leaf, block, witness and charging functions. Buffer
;; walk and session therefore share every leaf predicate and every state
;; machine; only the walk's control flow is duplicated.
(ns snug.vm.session
  (:require [kin.lang :refer [defn let local return set if while for do comment forever break defconst declarefn]]
            [snug.lang :refer [I32 Ext ext-none ints-none bytes-none Bool Bytes BytesW Ints IntsR + - * neg shl sar ushr bit-and bit-or
                               < > <= >= == != and or not u8 blen ia iset ilen]]
            [snug.cbor.codes :refer [CODE_TOO_LARGE CODE_NOT_MAP CODE_TRAILING CODE_TRUNCATED O_TOP O_MAX_BYTES
                                     O_ERR_POS O_HI O_LO O_PROFILE O_ITEMS O_MAX_ITEMS O_MAX_DEPTH PF_TAGS]]
            [snug.cbor.head :refer [fail head-size be16 be32 read-arg]]
            [snug.cbor.tags :refer [typed-size]]
            [snug.vm.layout :refer [HEADER_WORDS H_POOL_BYTES H_S_RULES VM_BUDGET VM_POS VM_FRAMES VM_RULE R_TYPE
                                    R_BUDGET R_INCONSISTENT H_FLAGS H_S_LEAVES FL_EXT FL_EMBED K_EXT VM_BUDGET_START
                                    H_LIM_INPUT R_GROUP_LIMIT R_AGROW VM_PBASE]]
            [snug.vm.base :refer [new-epoch q-add q-stamp ts-test cset-rec cset-width wit-empty wit-set]]
            [snug.vm.dead :refer [dead-item]]
            [snug.vm.eval :refer [eval-item]]
            [snug.vm.api :refer [vm-setup vm-output vm-witness-output lim arena-lease]]
            [snug.vm.arena :refer [arena-take arena-fit]]
            [snug.vm.sbase :refer [arena-gate arena-items VMS_NEED VMS_YIELD GO SS_PH SS_TOTAL SS_POS SS_NEED_OFF SS_NEED_LEN
                                   SS_QUANTUM SS_SP SS_RET SS_KEEP SS_ATOP SS_FRAMES SS_MAXF SS_CODE SS_WB0
                                   SS_WORK SS_CUT SS_CHN SS_CHAIN SS_PSTK SS_PCAP SS_PROG SS_RTS SS_RNQ
                                   SS_STEPS IT_POS IT_D IT_FB IT_CK IT_NQ IT_END IT_CTX IT_MODE IT_NOTE
                                   IT_PAIR SS_ABYTES SS_PROF SS_HDR PH_START PH_ITEM PH_RET PH_FRAME PH_DONE
                                   PH_HELD VMS_HELD VMS_RESUME SS_UNK SS_NPEND SS_PEND PW pend-raw pend-drop
                                   SS_SEQ SS_MLEN
                                   F_END F_KE F_KA
                                   MODE_ITEM MODE_VSEQ MODE_DSEQ MODE_FRAME FW FK_ARR FK_MAP FK_TAG FK_TEXT
                                   FK_BSTR FK_DARR FK_DMAP FK_DTEXT FK_DSEQ F_KIND F_PH F_PIN F_N F_EL
                                   nframes vms-session-words vms-arena-bytes fbase ftop fpop ret ensure
                                   need yld suspended must-yield cut-yield progress keys-save rebase chain-has prescan-run fits-known cross-known
                                   prescan str-stop big-req lits-need bstr-reads note-req note-put imin
                                   VMS_GROW SS_VNEED SS_GW SS_GB SS_GS SS_GA SS_VOK F_IND]]
            [snug.vm.sstr :refer [S_EMBRUN open-text text-run open-bstr bstr-run embed-ret]]
            [snug.cbor.canon :refer [targ head-short]]
            [snug.cbor.stdtags :refer [rule-tag typed-any-size]]
            [snug.cbor.keys :refer [key-end-any]]
            [snug.vm.svalid :refer [VI_NEED VI_GROW vsess vitem]]
            [snug.vm.scont :refer [M_KEY open-arr arr-start arr-run arr-ret open-darr open-dseq darr-run
                                   darr-ret open-map open-dmap map-next map-key map-ret open-tag tag-run
                                   tag-ret]]))

(declarefn vms-run)

;; a handler's "the session has finished" (SS_CODE holds the answer)
(defconst ^I32 FIN -66)

;; ------------------------------------------------------------ API

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-words [^IntsR p]
  (comment "Words of the session array (Ints): header, frames, prescan stack,"
           "crossing chain (D+6 of each).")
  (return (vms-session-words p)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-arena [^IntsR p ^IntsR limits ^I32 total]
  (comment "Bytes of the key arena (BytesW) a session on a message of `total` bytes"
           "starts with: at most 256 (D342). vms-step asks for more (VMS_GROW,"
           "vms-grow-arena) as the input it reads grows, up to vms-arena-bytes.")
  (return (imin (vms-arena-bytes p limits total) 256)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-init [^IntsR p ^Bytes pool ^I32 rule ^IntsR limits ^Ints s ^Ints ss ^BytesW ka
                           ^I32 total ^I32 quantum]
  (comment "Start a session on rule over a message of exactly `total` bytes: s is a"
           "VM scratch (vm-scratch-words, initialised as for vm-validate), ss the"
           "session array (vms-words), ka the key arena (vms-arena bytes), all"
           "owned by this session until it ends. quantum > 0 yields after about"
           "that many work units per step (D093); 0 never yields. 0, or -1 Program"
           "inconsistent (or a negative total or quantum), -2 an array too small,"
           "-3 rule out of range.")
  (if (< (ilen p) HEADER_WORDS) (return (neg 1)))
  (if (!= (ia p H_POOL_BYTES) (blen pool)) (return (neg 1)))
  (if (or (< total 0) (< quantum 0)) (return (neg 1)))
  (let [su (vm-setup p rule 0 0 0 limits s)]
    (if (< su 0) (return su)))
  (comment "the session's arena starts at the lease and grows on demand (arena-fit)")
  (arena-fit s (arena-lease p))
  (if (< (ilen ss) (vms-session-words p)) (return (neg 2)))
  (if (< (blen ka) (vms-arena p limits total)) (return (neg 2)))
  (let [nf (nframes p)]
    (for [^I32 k 0 SS_HDR] (iset ss k 0))
    (iset ss SS_PH PH_START)
    (iset ss SS_TOTAL total)
    (iset ss SS_QUANTUM quantum)
    (iset ss SS_FRAMES SS_HDR)
    (iset ss SS_MAXF nf)
    (iset ss SS_PSTK (+ SS_HDR (* nf FW)))
    (iset ss SS_PCAP nf)
    (iset ss SS_CHAIN (+ (+ SS_HDR (* nf FW)) (* 2 nf)))
    (iset ss SS_PEND (+ (+ SS_HDR (* nf FW)) (* 3 nf)))
    (iset ss SS_CHN (neg 1))
    (iset ss SS_ATOP 0)
    (comment "the key arena's bound (D342: ka itself may start smaller)")
    (iset ss SS_ABYTES (vms-arena-bytes p limits total))
    (iset ss SS_PROF (ia s O_PROFILE)))
  (return 0))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-unknown-total [^IntsR p ^IntsR limits]
  (comment "D085: the provisional end of an unknown-length session -- the effective input"
           "limit (more bytes than that is too_large); size its key arena for it.")
  (return (lim limits 2 (ia p H_LIM_INPUT))))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-init-unknown [^IntsR p ^Bytes pool ^I32 rule ^IntsR limits ^Ints s ^Ints ss ^BytesW ka
                                   ^I32 quantum]
  (comment "D085: a session over a message of UNKNOWN length (drain mode). It runs as"
           "a known-length session ending at the input limit, but every check that"
           "depends on the end is held: a length or count beyond the bytes seen is a"
           "pending check, a verdict is held (vms-step answers VMS_HELD, out filled),"
           "and vms-eof(n) settles both once the end is known -- so codes, offsets,"
           "budget and items are a buffer's of the same bytes. ka: vms-arena bytes for"
           "vms-unknown-total. Results as vms-init's.")
  (let [r (vms-init p pool rule limits s ss ka (vms-unknown-total p limits) quantum)]
    (if (< r 0) (return r))
    (iset ss SS_UNK 1)
    (return 0)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-init-seq [^IntsR p ^Bytes pool ^I32 rule ^IntsR limits ^Ints s ^Ints ss ^BytesW ka
                               ^I32 quantum]
  (comment "D212: a session over ONE MESSAGE OF A CBOR SEQUENCE (RFC 8742): an"
           "unknown-length session whose root's end is a boundary, not a trailing"
           "check. Offsets are relative to the message start. The verdict is held"
           "(VMS_HELD) while a pending end check is open or while it is truncated;"
           "later steps drop the checks their windows cover and answer it; vms-eof"
           "settles as in drain mode. vms-message-length: the root's end once it"
           "completed. Re-run on the same arrays for the next message. ka: vms-arena"
           "bytes for vms-unknown-total. Results as vms-init's.")
  (let [r (vms-init-unknown p pool rule limits s ss ka quantum)]
    (if (< r 0) (return r))
    (iset ss SS_SEQ 1)
    (iset ss SS_MLEN (neg 1))
    (return 0)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-message-length [^IntsR ss]
  (comment "D212: in a sequence session, the message's length (its root's end) once"
           "the root completed -- the next message starts there -- else -1.")
  (if (!= (ia ss SS_SEQ) 1) (return (neg 1)))
  (return (ia ss SS_MLEN)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-held-code [^IntsR ss]
  (comment "D085: after VMS_HELD, the held verdict's code (out holds it). A nonzero one"
           "is certainly a refusal of the whole message, though the buffer's code may"
           "then be truncated or too_large instead (fail-fast reports it at once).")
  (return (ia ss SS_CODE)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-need-offset [^IntsR ss]
  (return (ia ss SS_NEED_OFF)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-need-length [^IntsR ss]
  (return (ia ss SS_NEED_LEN)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-position [^IntsR ss]
  (comment "Where the walk stands after VMS_NEED or VMS_YIELD (absolute).")
  (return (ia ss SS_POS)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-keep [^IntsR ss]
  (comment "After VMS_NEED or VMS_YIELD: no byte before this offset will be asked"
           "for again, so a forward-only source may drop them. It is the position,"
           "or the start of a content that must be read twice (D094).")
  (return (ia ss SS_KEEP)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-steps [^IntsR ss]
  (return (ia ss SS_STEPS)))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------ the end

(defn ^Bool seq-holds [^IntsR ss]
  (comment "D212: a sequence message's verdict waits while a pending end check is open"
           "or while it is truncated (is the input longer than the provisional end?).")
  (return (or (> (ia ss SS_NPEND) 0) (== (ia ss SS_CODE) CODE_TRUNCATED))))

(defn settle [^Ints ss]
  (comment "The verdict is in out: done, or held while an unknown end is (D085); in a"
           "sequence only while seq-holds (D212).")
  (if (and (== (ia ss SS_SEQ) 1) (== (ia ss SS_UNK) 1))
    (do (if (seq-holds ss) (iset ss SS_PH PH_HELD) (iset ss SS_PH PH_DONE))
        (return)))
  (if (== (ia ss SS_UNK) 1) (iset ss SS_PH PH_HELD) (iset ss SS_PH PH_DONE)))

(defn ^I32 fin [^Ints s ^Ints ss ^Ints out ^I32 base ^I32 code ^I32 sub ^I32 off]
  (comment "The verdict: the scratch back to absolute offsets, out filled (off is"
           "window-relative), the session done.")
  (rebase s base)
  (vm-output s out code sub (+ off base))
  (iset ss SS_CODE code)
  (settle ss)
  (return FIN))

(defn ^I32 fin-bad [^Ints s ^Ints ss ^I32 base]
  (comment "The Program is inconsistent with its scratch (vm-validate's -1).")
  (rebase s base)
  (iset ss SS_CODE (neg 1))
  (iset ss SS_PH PH_DONE)
  (return FIN))

(defn ^I32 doc-start [^IntsR p ^Bytes b ^Ints s ^Ints ss ^Ints out ^I32 base ^I32 wend]
  (comment "vm-run's start: too_large, not_map, the rule's typeset as the root's"
           "query; then the root item.")
  (let [n (ia ss SS_TOTAL)
        at (- 0 base)]
    (if (> n (ia s O_MAX_BYTES))
      (do (fail s at CODE_TOO_LARGE)
          (return (fin s ss out base CODE_TOO_LARGE 0 at))))
    (if (== (ia s O_TOP) 0)
      (do (if (== n 0)
            (do (fail s at CODE_NOT_MAP)
                (return (fin s ss out base CODE_NOT_MAP 0 at))))
          (let [g (ensure ss base wend at (+ at 1))]
            (if (suspended g) (return g)))
          (if (!= (ushr (u8 b at) 5) 5)
            (do (fail s at CODE_NOT_MAP)
                (return (fin s ss out base CODE_NOT_MAP 0 at))))))
    (let [rr (+ (ia p H_S_RULES) (* 5 (ia s VM_RULE)))
          ts (ia p (+ rr 2))
          cr (cset-rec p s 0)
          w (ia p cr)
          frames (ia s VM_FRAMES)
          e (new-epoch s)
          nq (q-add p s frames w 0 ts e at)]
      (if (== nq (neg R_BUDGET))
        (do (let [vp (ia s VM_POS)]
              (return (fin s ss out base R_BUDGET 0 vp)))))
      (if (< nq 0) (return (fin-bad s ss base)))
      (iset ss SS_RTS ts)
      (iset ss SS_RNQ nq)
      (iset ss IT_POS 0)
      (iset ss IT_D 0)
      (iset ss IT_FB frames)
      (iset ss IT_CK 0)
      (iset ss IT_NQ nq)
      (iset ss IT_END n)
      (iset ss IT_CTX 0)
      (iset ss IT_MODE MODE_ITEM)
      (iset ss IT_NOTE (neg 1))
      (iset ss IT_PAIR (neg 1))
      (iset ss SS_PH PH_ITEM)
      (return GO))))

(defn ^I32 root-end [^IntsR p ^Ints s ^Ints ss ^Ints out ^I32 base ^I32 wend]
  (comment "vm-run's end: a code, trailing bytes, else the root's typeset test and"
           "the witness.")
  (let [r (ia ss SS_RET)
        n (ia ss SS_TOTAL)
        at (- 0 base)]
    (if (== r (neg R_BUDGET))
      (do (let [vp (ia s VM_POS)]
            (return (fin s ss out base R_BUDGET 0 vp)))))
    (if (or (== r (neg R_INCONSISTENT)) (== r (neg R_AGROW))) (return (fin-bad s ss base)))
    (if (== r (neg R_GROUP_LIMIT))
      (do (let [vg (ia s VM_POS)]
            (return (fin s ss out base R_GROUP_LIMIT 0 vg)))))
    (if (< r 0)
      (do (let [ep (ia s O_ERR_POS)]
            (return (fin s ss out base (neg r) 0 ep)))))
    (comment "D212: in a sequence the root's end is the message's boundary: no trailing"
             "check, nothing read or asked past it.")
    (if (== (ia ss SS_SEQ) 1) (iset ss SS_MLEN r))
    (comment "D085: with the end unknown, a byte after the root is trailing; with none"
             "in the window yet, ask for one -- vms-eof tells it is the end.")
    (if (and (and (== (ia ss SS_UNK) 1) (!= r n)) (!= (ia ss SS_SEQ) 1))
      (do (if (< (- r base) wend)
            (do (fail s (- r base) CODE_TRAILING)
                (return (fin s ss out base CODE_TRAILING 0 (- r base)))))
          (return (need ss base (- r base) 1))))
    (if (and (!= r n) (!= (ia ss SS_SEQ) 1))
      (do (fail s (- r base) CODE_TRAILING)
          (return (fin s ss out base CODE_TRAILING 0 (- r base)))))
    (let [frames (ia s VM_FRAMES)
          w (cset-width p (cset-rec p s 0))
          nq (ia ss SS_RNQ)
          ts (ia ss SS_RTS)
          ev (q-stamp s frames w nq at)]
      (if (< ev 0)
        (do (let [vp1 (ia s VM_POS)]
              (return (fin s ss out base R_BUDGET 0 vp1)))))
      (let [t (ts-test p s ts ev at)]
        (if (< t 0)
          (do (let [vp2 (ia s VM_POS)]
                (return (fin s ss out base R_BUDGET 0 vp2)))))
        (if (== t 1) (return (fin s ss out base 0 0 at)))
        (if (wit-empty s) (wit-set s R_TYPE 0 0 (neg 1) 0 at))
        (rebase s base)
        (let [code (vm-witness-output s out)]
          (iset ss SS_CODE code)
          (settle ss)
          (return FIN))))))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------ one item

(defn ^I32 bstr-claim [^Bytes b ^Ints s ^I32 pos ^I32 end]
  (comment "D085: the content end the byte string's head at pos (in the window) claims,"
           "when the walk's take-len passes it against the provisional end, else -1."
           "Touches only O_HI/O_LO/O_ERR_POS, which the walk then sets again.")
  (if (or (>= pos end) (>= pos (blen b))) (return (neg 1)))
  (let [ai (bit-and (u8 b pos) 31)
        ^:mut q (+ pos 1)
        ^:mut hi 0
        ^:mut lo ai]
    (if (> ai 27) (return (neg 1)))
    (if (> (+ pos (head-size ai)) (blen b)) (return (neg 1)))
    (if (!= (ushr (u8 b pos) 5) 2) (return (neg 1)))
    (if (>= ai 24)
      (do (set q (read-arg b s pos ai end))
          (if (< q 0) (return (neg 1)))
          (set hi (ia s O_HI))
          (set lo (ia s O_LO))))
    (if (or (!= hi 0) (< lo 0)) (return (neg 1)))
    (if (> lo (- end q)) (return (neg 1)))
    (return (+ q lo))))

(defn ^I32 skip-bstr [^IntsR p ^Bytes pool ^Bytes b ^Ints s ^Ints ss ^I32 base ^I32 pos ^I32 hp ^I32 d
                      ^I32 fb ^I32 ck ^I32 nq ^I32 end ^I32 ctx ^Ext ext]
  (comment "D085: a byte string the walk takes from its head alone (no leaf reads its"
           "content), in an unknown-length session: as the buffer walk, plus the"
           "pending check of its length when its content passes the window. The walk's"
           "prologue (visit, count, head) comes first: the check is reached exactly"
           "when the visit's unit is there and the item count stays in its limit.")
  (comment "hp: the byte string's head -- pos, or pos + 1 for a bignum's content.")
  (let [claim (bstr-claim b s hp end)
        used0 (- (ia s VM_BUDGET_START) (ia s VM_BUDGET))
        items0 (ia s O_ITEMS)
        reach (and (and (>= (ia s VM_BUDGET) 1) (<= (+ items0 1) (ia s O_MAX_ITEMS)))
                   (or (== hp pos) (< d (ia s O_MAX_DEPTH))))]
    (local ^I32 r)
    (if (and (> claim (blen b)) (and (> nq 0) (!= hp pos)))
      (do (comment "a live bignum: its tag's filter and number tests come first, so take"
                   "the check's moment from a trial walk ending at the window (it stops at"
                   "the content's length, truncated), then undo what the trial changed"
                   "(the query flags it sets are set again alike)")
          (let [bud (ia s VM_BUDGET)
                vpos (ia s VM_POS)
                epos (ia s O_ERR_POS)
                tr (eval-item p pool b s pos d fb ck nq (blen b) ctx ext)]
            (if (and (== tr (neg CODE_TRUNCATED)) (== (ia s O_ERR_POS) hp))
              (pend-raw ss (+ claim base) (+ hp base) (- (ia s VM_BUDGET_START) (ia s VM_BUDGET)) (ia s O_ITEMS)))
            (iset s VM_BUDGET bud)
            (iset s VM_POS vpos)
            (iset s O_ERR_POS epos)
            (iset s O_ITEMS items0))
          (return (ret ss base (eval-item p pool b s pos d fb ck nq end ctx ext)))))
    (if (> nq 0)
      (set r (eval-item p pool b s pos d fb ck nq end ctx ext))
      (set r (dead-item b s pos d end)))
    (if (and reach (> claim (blen b)))
      (pend-raw ss (+ claim base) (+ hp base) (+ used0 1) (+ items0 1)))
    (return (ret ss base r))))

(defn ^I32 note-live [^Bytes b ^Ints ss ^I32 base ^I32 pos ^I32 end ^I32 wend ^I32 nk ^I32 req]
  (comment "D212 liveness: a tag-40 shape or data note (nk 2, 3) asks for a fixed span"
           "(73, 11 bytes) from the element; when the element already ends in the"
           "window (note-put reads nothing past it) the window suffices; else ask for"
           "one more byte of it, never for bytes past its own end.")
  (if (or (<= req wend) (and (!= nk 2) (!= nk 3))) (return req))
  (let [w (prescan b ss base pos end wend)]
    (iset ss SS_CHN (neg 1))
    (if (== w 1) (return wend))
    (return (+ wend 1))))

(defn ^I32 ext-need [^IntsR p ^IntsR s ^I32 fb ^I32 nq]
  (comment "D140: the largest maximum item size of the EXT leaves in the query list"
           "(their mask admits every item), or -1 when it has none.")
  (if (== (bit-and (ia p H_FLAGS) FL_EXT) 0) (return (neg 1)))
  (let [lv (ia p H_S_LEAVES)
        ^:mut m (neg 1)]
    (for [^I32 i 0 nq]
      (let [lb (+ lv (* 8 (ia s (+ fb i))))]
        (if (and (== (bit-and (ia p lb) 255) K_EXT) (> (ia p (+ lb 5)) m))
          (set m (ia p (+ lb 5))))))
    (return m)))

(defn ^I32 sib-rem [^IntsR ss]
  (comment "The items the top frame still owes from the pending one on (it"
           "included), for the sibling prescan; -1: up to the end.")
  (if (== (ia ss SS_SP) 0) (return 1))
  (let [f (ftop ss)
        kind (ia ss (+ f F_KIND))
        n (ia ss (+ f F_N))
        el (ia ss (+ f F_EL))]
    (comment "an indefinite container (D266): its siblings run to its break")
    (if (== (ia ss (+ f F_IND)) 1) (return (neg 1)))
    (if (or (== kind FK_ARR) (== kind FK_DARR))
      (do (if (< n 0) (return (neg 1)))
          (return (- n el))))
    (if (== kind FK_DSEQ) (return (neg 1)))
    (if (or (== kind FK_MAP) (== kind FK_DMAP)) (return (- (* 2 (- n el)) 1)))
    (return 1)))

(defn ^I32 tag-number [^Bytes b ^I32 pos]
  (comment "The number of the tag whose (valid-sized) head is at pos, -1 past 31 bits.")
  (let [ai (bit-and (u8 b pos) 31)]
    (if (< ai 24) (return ai))
    (if (== ai 24) (return (u8 b (+ pos 1))))
    (if (== ai 25) (return (be16 b (+ pos 1))))
    (return (neg 1))))

(defn ^I32 item-begin [^IntsR p ^Bytes pool ^Bytes b ^Ints s ^Ints ss ^BytesW ka ^Ints vs ^BytesW cb ^I32 base
                      ^I32 wend ^Ext ext]
  (comment "The pending item: its head (and any note or bounded piece it must have"
           "whole) in the window, then whole by the buffer walk when the window"
           "holds everything it can read, else a frame.")
  (let [pos (- (ia ss IT_POS) base)
        end (- (ia ss IT_END) base)
        d (ia ss IT_D)
        fb (ia ss IT_FB)
        ck (ia ss IT_CK)
        nq (ia ss IT_NQ)
        ctx (ia ss IT_CTX)
        mode (ia ss IT_MODE)
        note (ia ss IT_NOTE)
        pair (ia ss IT_PAIR)
        cut (- (ia ss SS_CUT) base)]
    (if (== mode MODE_VSEQ)
      (return (arr-start p b s ss ka base pos pos (neg 1) d fb ck nq end 0 (neg 1))))
    (if (== mode MODE_DSEQ) (return (open-dseq b ss ka base pos d end)))
    (if (cut-yield s ss (+ pos base)) (return (yld ss base pos)))
    (if (>= pos end)
      (do (progress ss 1)
          (if (> nq 0) (return (ret ss base (eval-item p pool b s pos d fb ck nq end ctx ext))))
          (return (ret ss base (dead-item b s pos d end)))))
    (if (or (< pos 0) (>= pos wend)) (return (need ss base pos 1)))
    (let [ib (u8 b pos)
          major (ushr ib 5)
          ai (bit-and ib 31)
          ^:mut h 1
          ^:mut direct 0]
      (if (<= ai 27) (set h (head-size ai)))
      (let [g (ensure ss base wend pos (+ pos (imin h (- end pos))))]
        (if (suspended g) (return g)))
      (if (>= note 0)
        (do (let [tf (fbase ss (sar note 2))
                  nk (bit-and note 3)
                  req0 (note-req b s nk pos end wend)
                  req (note-live b ss base pos end wend nk req0)
                  g2 (ensure ss base wend pos req)]
              (if (suspended g2) (return g2))
              (note-put b s ss nk pos end wend tf)
              (iset ss IT_NOTE (neg 1)))))
      (comment "what the walk may read, decided without charging anything: 1 the"
               "buffer walk takes it whole, -1 a frame, 0 the prescan decides")
      (if (== mode MODE_FRAME) (set direct (neg 1)))
      (comment "P8.4 (D265): above the Bindle tag set a tag 4 / 40 has the RFC rules the"
               "buffer walk applies to its content array (any count): whole, asked for whole")
      (if (and (and (== direct 0) (not (vsess s ss))) (and (== major 6) (and (<= ai 27) (<= (+ pos h) end))))
        (if (!= (bit-and (ia s O_PROFILE) PF_TAGS) 0)
          (do (targ b s pos)
              (let [rt1 (rule-tag (ia s O_HI) (ia s O_LO))]
                (if (or (== rt1 4) (== rt1 40))
                  (do (let [kx1 (key-end-any b pos end wend)]
                        (if (< kx1 (neg 1)) (return (need ss base pos (- (- (neg 2) kx1) pos)))))
                      (set direct 1)))))))
      (comment "P8.4 (D266): with the valid machinery, an item the frames do not take is"
               "whole: a malformed head, an indefinite string, and the tags whose rules"
               "read their content (bignums, 4, 40, typed arrays, 0, 24, 32)")
      (if (and (== direct 0) (vsess s ss))
        (do (if (or (and (>= ai 28) (<= ai 30)) (and (== ai 31) (or (<= major 3) (>= major 6))))
              (set direct 1))
            (if (and (== direct 0) (and (== major 6) (and (<= ai 27) (<= (+ pos h) end))))
              (do (targ b s pos)
                  (let [rt0 (rule-tag (ia s O_HI) (ia s O_LO))]
                    (if (or (or (or (== rt0 0) (== rt0 24)) (or (== rt0 32) (or (== rt0 2) (== rt0 3))))
                            (or (or (== rt0 4) (== rt0 40)) (or (> (typed-size rt0) 0) (> (typed-any-size rt0) 0))))
                      (set direct 1)))))))
      (if (and (== direct 0) (<= end cut)) (set direct 1))
      (if (and (== direct 0) (or (<= major 1) (== major 7))) (set direct 1))
      (if (and (== direct 0) (and (== major 2) (== nq 0))) (set direct 1))
      (if (and (== direct 0) (and (== major 6) (or (== ib 194) (== ib 195))))
        (do (let [req2 (big-req b s pos end wend)]
              (if (> req2 wend) (return (need ss base pos (- req2 pos)))))
            (set direct 1)))
      (if (and (== direct 0) (and (== major 6) (and (and (== nq 0) (== ai 24)) (!= (ia ss SS_UNK) 1))))
        (do (let [tn (tag-number b pos)
                  x (+ pos 2)]
              (if (and (> (typed-size tn) 0) (< tn 84))
                (do (comment "dead-typed reads only its content's head")
                    (if (< x end)
                      (do (let [g5 (ensure ss base wend pos (+ x 1))]
                            (if (suspended g5) (return g5)))
                          (let [ai5 (bit-and (u8 b x) 31)
                                ^:mut h5 1]
                            (if (<= ai5 27) (set h5 (head-size ai5)))
                            (let [g6 (ensure ss base wend pos (+ x (imin h5 (- end x))))]
                              (if (suspended g6) (return g6))))))
                    (set direct 1))))))
      (if (and (== direct 0) (and (<= major 3) (> nq 0)))
        (do (let [stop (str-stop b pos end)]
              (if (< stop 0) (set direct 1))
              (if (>= stop 0)
                (do (let [^:mut cls 8]
                      (if (== major 2) (set cls 4))
                      (let [ln (lits-need p s fb nq cls (- stop pos))]
                        (if (< ln 0)
                          (do (let [g3 (ensure ss base wend pos stop)]
                                (if (suspended g3) (return g3)))
                              (set direct 1))
                          (do (let [g4 (ensure ss base wend pos (+ pos ln))]
                                (if (suspended g4) (return g4)))
                              (if (and (== major 2) (not (bstr-reads p s fb nq (- stop (+ pos h)))))
                                (set direct 1)))))))))))
      (if (== direct 0)
        (do (let [at (+ pos base)]
              (if (cross-known ss at) (set direct (neg 1)))
              (if (and (== direct 0) (fits-known ss at)) (set direct 1))
              (if (== direct 0)
                (do (let [pr (prescan-run b ss base pos end cut (sib-rem ss))]
                      (if (< pr 0)
                        (do (if (== (prescan b ss base pos end cut) 1) (set direct 1) (set direct (neg 1)))
                            (iset ss SS_CHN (neg 1)))
                        (if (fits-known ss at) (set direct 1) (set direct (neg 1))))))))))
      (comment "D140: an item an EXT leaf may judge is taken whole when it is no longer"
               "than the leaves' largest maximum: ask for that much from its start;"
               "if it still crosses, it is longer, every such leaf fails by size, and"
               "the walk goes on as decided: whatever it reads, every EXT leaf fails by"
               "size before asking. (direct 1 alone does not mean whole: a byte string no"
               "leaf reads is walked from its head, so this runs whatever direct is.)")
      (if (> nq 0)
        (do (let [xm (ext-need p s fb nq)]
              (if (>= xm 0)
                (do (let [xreq (+ pos (imin xm (- end pos)))]
                      (comment "D212 liveness: before asking for the leaves' maximum, take the"
                               "item whole if it already ends in the window; else ask for one"
                               "more byte of it (never for bytes past its own end)")
                      (if (> xreq wend)
                        (do (if (!= (prescan b ss base pos end wend) 1)
                              (do (iset ss SS_CHN (neg 1))
                                  (return (need ss base pos (+ (- wend pos) 1)))))
                            (set direct 1))
                        (if (== (prescan b ss base pos end xreq) 1) (set direct 1)))
                      (iset ss SS_CHN (neg 1))))))))
      (comment "P8.5: an item taken whole may push on the group arena up to its bytes'"
               "bound: room first (a suspension point, nothing charged yet)")
      (if (== direct 1)
        (do (let [g7 (arena-gate p s ss (arena-items p s (- (imin end wend) pos)) (+ (imin end wend) base))]
              (if (== g7 VMS_GROW) (return g7)))))
      (progress ss 1)
      (if (and (== direct 1) (vsess s ss))
        (if (not (and (and (== major 2) (or (== nq 0) (== (bit-and (ia p H_FLAGS) FL_EMBED) 0)))
                      (and (and (<= ai 27) (<= (+ pos h) end)) (head-short b pos))))
          (do (let [rv (vitem p pool b s ss vs cb pos d fb ck nq end wend ctx ext)]
                (if (== rv VI_NEED) (return (need ss base pos (ia ss SS_VNEED))))
                (if (== rv VI_GROW) (return VMS_GROW))
                (return (ret ss base rv))))))
      (if (and (== direct 1) (and (== major 2) (== (ia ss SS_UNK) 1)))
        (return (skip-bstr p pool b s ss base pos pos d fb ck nq end ctx ext)))
      (comment "D085: a bignum decided from its content's head (big-req) claims its content too")
      (if (and (== direct 1) (and (and (== major 6) (or (== ib 194) (== ib 195))) (== (ia ss SS_UNK) 1)))
        (return (skip-bstr p pool b s ss base pos (+ pos 1) d fb ck nq end ctx ext)))
      (if (== direct 1)
        (do (if (> nq 0) (return (ret ss base (eval-item p pool b s pos d fb ck nq end ctx ext))))
            (return (ret ss base (dead-item b s pos d end)))))
      (if (== major 2) (return (open-bstr p pool b s ss ka base pos d fb ck nq end ctx 0 0 0)))
      (if (== major 3) (return (open-text p pool b s ss ka base pos d fb ck nq end ctx)))
      (if (== major 4)
        (do (if (> nq 0) (return (open-arr p b s ss ka base pos d fb ck nq end ctx pair)))
            (return (open-darr p b s ss ka base pos d end pair))))
      (if (== major 5)
        (do (if (> nq 0) (return (open-map p b s ss ka base pos d fb ck nq end ctx)))
            (return (open-dmap p b s ss ka base pos d end))))
      (return (open-tag p b s ss ka base pos d fb ck nq end ctx)))))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------ returns and frames

(defn ^I32 deliver [^IntsR p ^Bytes b ^Ints s ^Ints ss ^Ints out ^I32 base ^I32 wend]
  (comment "An item returned (SS_RET): to the top frame, or the root's end. A"
           "negated code unwinds frame by frame, as every caller of the buffer walk"
           "returns it at once, except that a byte string running an EMBED"
           "sub-walk catches an inner profile or limit refusal (embed-run).")
  (let [sp (ia ss SS_SP)
        r (ia ss SS_RET)]
    (if (== sp 0) (return (root-end p s ss out base wend)))
    (let [f (ftop ss)
          kind (ia ss (+ f F_KIND))]
      (if (< r 0)
        (do (if (and (and (and (!= r (neg R_BUDGET)) (!= r (neg R_INCONSISTENT)))
                          (and (!= r (neg R_GROUP_LIMIT)) (!= r (neg R_AGROW))))
                     (and (== kind FK_BSTR) (== (ia ss (+ f F_PH)) S_EMBRUN)))
              (return (embed-ret p s ss base f r)))
            (fpop ss)
            (return GO)))
      (if (== kind FK_ARR) (return (arr-ret p s ss base f r 0)))
      (if (or (== kind FK_DARR) (== kind FK_DSEQ)) (return (darr-ret ss f r)))
      (if (or (== kind FK_MAP) (== kind FK_DMAP)) (return (map-ret p s ss base f r 0)))
      (if (== kind FK_TAG) (return (tag-ret b s ss base f r)))
      (if (== kind FK_BSTR) (return (embed-ret p s ss base f r)))
      (return (fin-bad s ss base)))))

(defn ^I32 frame-run [^IntsR p ^Bytes pool ^Bytes b ^Ints s ^Ints ss ^BytesW ka ^Ints vs ^BytesW cb ^I32 base
                     ^I32 wend ^Ext ext]
  (let [f (ftop ss)
        kind (ia ss (+ f F_KIND))]
    (if (== kind FK_ARR) (return (arr-run p pool b s ss vs cb base f ext)))
    (if (or (== kind FK_DARR) (== kind FK_DSEQ)) (return (darr-run p pool b s ss vs cb base f ext)))
    (if (or (== kind FK_MAP) (== kind FK_DMAP))
      (do (if (== (ia ss (+ f F_PH)) M_KEY) (return (map-key p pool b s ss ka vs cb base wend f ext)))
          (return (map-next p pool b s ss ka vs cb base wend f ext))))
    (if (== kind FK_TAG) (return (tag-run p pool b s ss ka base wend f ext)))
    (if (or (== kind FK_TEXT) (== kind FK_DTEXT)) (return (text-run p pool b s ss base wend f ext)))
    (if (== kind FK_BSTR) (return (bstr-run p pool b s ss base wend f ext)))
    (return (fin-bad s ss base))))

(defn ^I32 keep-of [^IntsR ss]
  (comment "vms-keep: the position, or the earliest pinned content start.")
  (let [^:mut k (ia ss SS_POS)
        sp (ia ss SS_SP)]
    (for [^I32 i 0 sp]
      (let [pin (ia ss (+ (fbase ss i) F_PIN))]
        (if (and (>= pin 0) (< pin k)) (set k pin))))
    (return k)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-step-x [^IntsR p ^Bytes pool ^Bytes b ^Ints s ^Ints ss ^BytesW ka ^Ints out ^I32 base ^Ext ext]
  (comment "vms-step-v without the valid machinery's buffers: a valid-CBOR or any-key"
           "run walks as before P8.4 (non-deterministic encodings refused, duplicates"
           "bytewise). For hosts that have not moved to vms-step-v.")
  (iset ss SS_VOK 0)
  (return (vms-run p pool b s ss ka out base ext (ints-none) (bytes-none))))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-step-v [^IntsR p ^Bytes pool ^Bytes b ^Ints s ^Ints ss ^BytesW ka ^Ints out ^I32 base ^Ext ext
                             ^Ints vs ^BytesW cb]
  (comment "vms-step-x with the valid machinery (P8.4, D266): vs (Ints) and cb"
           "(BytesW) are the host's buffers for whole items' canonical path, any"
           "length. Answers as vms-step-x, and VMS_GROW: grow the arrays"
           "vms-grow-words / -bytes / -scratch / -arena name (keeping S's and the"
           "arena's contents), then step again over the same window.")
  (iset ss SS_VOK 1)
  (return (vms-run p pool b s ss ka out base ext vs cb)))

(defn ^I32 vms-run [^IntsR p ^Bytes pool ^Bytes b ^Ints s ^Ints ss ^BytesW ka ^Ints out ^I32 base ^Ext ext
                    ^Ints vs ^BytesW cb]
  (comment "Run the session over the window b, message bytes from base. Answers the"
           "verdict's code (>= 0; out filled as by vm-validate: absolute offsets),"
           "VMS_NEED (give a window holding [vms-need-offset, + vms-need-length)),"
           "VMS_YIELD (give a window holding vms-position; nothing else changed),"
           "or -1 Program inconsistent / a negative base, -4 out shorter than 8"
           "words. After the verdict every call answers it again.")
  (if (< (ilen out) 8) (return (neg 4)))
  (if (== (ia ss SS_PH) PH_DONE) (return (ia ss SS_CODE)))
  (if (and (== (ia ss SS_PH) PH_HELD) (and (== (ia ss SS_SEQ) 1) (>= base 0)))
    (do (comment "D212: the window's bytes exist; once no claim is open the verdict stands")
        (pend-drop ss (+ base (blen b)))
        (if (not (seq-holds ss))
          (do (iset ss SS_PH PH_DONE)
              (return (ia ss SS_CODE))))))
  (if (== (ia ss SS_PH) PH_HELD) (return VMS_HELD))
  (if (< base 0) (return (neg 1)))
  (comment "D342: the key arena grows with the input read. Every key it holds is a"
           "disjoint span of the message read so far, and a copy is made only of"
           "bytes in a window, so the window's end bounds what this step can write"
           "(the valid machinery's keys ask for themselves, vgrow). Nothing has"
           "changed yet: the host grows ka and steps again.")
  (let [an (imin (ia ss SS_ABYTES) (+ base (blen b)))]
    (if (> an (blen ka))
      (do (let [^:mut g (imin (ia ss SS_ABYTES) (* 2 (blen ka)))]
            (if (< g an) (set g an))
            (iset ss SS_GW 0)
            (iset ss SS_GB 0)
            (iset ss SS_GS 0)
            (iset ss SS_GA g))
          (return VMS_GROW))))
  (if (== (ia ss SS_UNK) 1) (pend-drop ss (+ base (blen b))))
  (let [wend (blen b)
        q (ia ss SS_QUANTUM)
        pos0 (- (ia ss SS_POS) base)
        ^:mut cut wend]
    (rebase s (neg base))
    (comment "P8.5: S grown for the group arena (VMS_GROW) -- the arena takes the words"
             "it asked for, its chunk heap moved up (program-2 §9.4 relocation)")
    (arena-take s)
    (iset s VM_PBASE base)
    (iset ss SS_GW 0)
    (iset ss SS_GB 0)
    (iset ss SS_GS 0)
    (iset ss SS_GA 0)
    (iset ss SS_WB0 (ia s VM_BUDGET))
    (iset ss SS_WORK 0)
    (iset ss SS_PROG 0)
    (iset ss SS_CHN (neg 1))
    (iset ss SS_STEPS (+ (ia ss SS_STEPS) 1))
    (if (> q 0)
      (do (let [^:mut c2 (+ pos0 q)]
            (if (< c2 (+ pos0 1)) (set c2 (+ pos0 1)))
            (if (< c2 cut) (set cut c2)))))
    (iset ss SS_CUT (+ cut base))
    (forever
      (let [ph (ia ss SS_PH)]
        (local ^I32 r)
        (if (== ph PH_ITEM)
          (set r (item-begin p pool b s ss ka vs cb base wend ext))
          (if (== ph PH_RET)
            (set r (deliver p b s ss out base wend))
            (if (== ph PH_FRAME)
              (set r (frame-run p pool b s ss ka vs cb base wend ext))
              (if (== ph PH_START)
                (set r (doc-start p b s ss out base wend))
                (return (ia ss SS_CODE))))))
        (if (== r FIN)
          (do (if (== (ia ss SS_PH) PH_HELD) (return VMS_HELD))
              (return (ia ss SS_CODE))))
        (if (or (suspended r) (== r VMS_GROW))
          (do (keys-save b ss ka base)
              (rebase s base)
              (iset ss SS_KEEP (keep-of ss))
              (return r)))))))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-step [^IntsR p ^Bytes pool ^Bytes b ^Ints s ^Ints ss ^BytesW ka ^Ints out ^I32 base]
  (comment "vms-step-x with no extension controls (D140).")
  (return (vms-step-x p pool b s ss ka out base (ext-none))))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-grow-words [^IntsR ss]
  (comment "P8.4 (D266): after VMS_GROW, the words the valid scratch vs must have (0:"
           "enough).")
  (return (ia ss SS_GW)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-grow-bytes [^IntsR ss]
  (comment "After VMS_GROW, the bytes the canonical buffer cb must have (0: enough).")
  (return (ia ss SS_GB)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-grow-scratch [^IntsR ss]
  (comment "After VMS_GROW, the words S must have (0: enough; keep its contents).")
  (return (ia ss SS_GS)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-grow-arena [^IntsR ss]
  (comment "After VMS_GROW, the bytes the key arena must have (0: enough; keep its"
           "contents).")
  (return (ia ss SS_GA)))

(defn ^:pub ^I32 vms-eof [^Ints ss ^Ints out ^I32 n]
  (comment "D085: the message of an unknown-length session ended after n bytes (or has"
           "passed the input limit: n is then any count above it). Settles what was"
           "pending: too_large past the limit; else the earliest check whose claim n"
           "does not cover (truncated, as the buffer walk answers there); else a held"
           "verdict stands. Answers the code (out filled), or VMS_RESUME when the walk"
           "was waiting for bytes: the ends it carries become n -- step again over the"
           "bytes from vms-keep to n, and it finishes without asking past n.")
  (if (< (ilen out) 8) (return (neg 4)))
  (if (== (ia ss SS_PH) PH_DONE) (return (ia ss SS_CODE)))
  (if (!= (ia ss SS_UNK) 1) (return (neg 1)))
  (let [total (ia ss SS_TOTAL)]
    (if (or (< n 0) (> n total))
      (do (for [^I32 z 0 8] (iset out z 0))
          (iset out 0 CODE_TOO_LARGE)
          (iset ss SS_CODE CODE_TOO_LARGE)
          (iset ss SS_PH PH_DONE)
          (return CODE_TOO_LARGE)))
    (pend-drop ss n)
    (if (> (ia ss SS_NPEND) 0)
      (do (let [at (ia ss SS_PEND)]
            (for [^I32 z2 0 8] (iset out z2 0))
            (iset out 0 CODE_TRUNCATED)
            (iset out 2 (ia ss (+ at 1)))
            (iset out 3 (ia ss (+ at 2)))
            (iset out 4 (ia ss (+ at 3)))
            (iset ss SS_CODE CODE_TRUNCATED)
            (iset ss SS_PH PH_DONE)
            (return CODE_TRUNCATED))))
    (if (== (ia ss SS_PH) PH_HELD)
      (do (iset ss SS_PH PH_DONE)
          (return (ia ss SS_CODE))))
    (comment "waiting for bytes: every end that was the provisional one is now n")
    (let [sp (ia ss SS_SP)]
      (for [^I32 i 0 sp]
        (let [fi (fbase ss i)]
          (if (== (ia ss (+ fi F_END)) total) (iset ss (+ fi F_END) n))))
      (if (== (ia ss IT_END) total) (iset ss IT_END n))
      (comment "a crossing map key being copied past n: its pair goes on over the copy"
               "(head included), ending at n -- the buffer walk's key past its end")
      (if (> sp 0)
        (do (let [f (ftop ss)
                  kind (ia ss (+ f F_KIND))]
              (if (and (or (== kind FK_MAP) (== kind FK_DMAP))
                       (and (== (ia ss (+ f F_PH)) M_KEY) (> (ia ss (+ f F_KE)) n)))
                (iset ss (+ f F_KE) (neg 1)))))))
    (iset ss SS_TOTAL n)
    (iset ss SS_UNK 2)
    (return VMS_RESUME)))
